WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.467 --> 00:00:14.389
We were in a store. and a guy in that
store told us to put our uniforms on.

2
00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:17.726
"What the hell are you talking about?"

3
00:00:17.976 --> 00:00:22.523
He says. "The U.S.A.'s
in a war with Japan".

4
00:00:22.773 --> 00:00:24.233
We couldn't believe it.

5
00:00:24.483 --> 00:00:27.444
Our country was attacked.
It's a different...

6
00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:31.949
It wasn't like Korea or Vietnam.
We was attacked.

7
00:00:32.199 --> 00:00:35.244
And. you know. it was a feeling of...

8
00:00:35.494 --> 00:00:39.414
Maybe we're just dumb country
people where I come from...

9
00:00:39.665 --> 00:00:41.750
...but a lot of us volunteered.

10
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.630
"Who would like to volunteer
for the Tank Corps? For the Air Force?

11
00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:49.967
For the Navy?" Or whatever.

12
00:00:50.217 --> 00:00:54.179
Then they said. "Who would
volunteer for the Airborne?"

13
00:00:54.429 --> 00:00:57.307
So I says.
"What the hell's the Airborne?"

14
00:00:57.558 --> 00:01:00.060
We came from a small. small town...

15
00:01:00.310 --> 00:01:05.691
...and three fellows in that town
that were 4-F committed suicide.

16
00:01:05.941 --> 00:01:09.862
Because they couldn't go.
A different time.

17
00:01:10.112 --> 00:01:13.740
I did things. I didn't do them
for medals or accolades.

18
00:01:13.991 --> 00:01:18.036
I did them because they...
It's what had to be done.

19
00:01:18.287 --> 00:01:24.334
The guy says. "You jump out
of airplanes to fight the enemy."

20
00:01:24.585 --> 00:01:28.338
These guys said. "Go to hell."
Nobody put up their hands.

21
00:01:28.589 --> 00:01:31.175
And I don't know
what brought it up...

22
00:01:31.425 --> 00:01:35.929
...but the guy speaking said.
"You get paid $50 a month more."

23
00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:40.017
So that made it 100 bucks.

24
00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:48.074
Support us and become VIP member 
to remove all ads from www.OpenSubtitles.org

25
00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:43.575
Okay. boys. let's get
this gear stowed.

26
00:05:01.885 --> 00:05:07.349
Fox Company. we go in five.

27
00:05:08.851 --> 00:05:12.729
- Sergeant Maynard?
- Nope.

28
00:05:13.522 --> 00:05:17.568
In the name of the Father
and the Son...

29
00:05:22.406 --> 00:05:24.950
1st Platoon. draw small arms.

30
00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:28.036
It'll be too late when
you face the enemy.

31
00:05:28.287 --> 00:05:30.414
Easy Company!

32
00:05:30.664 --> 00:05:33.584
Listen up! Gather up around me!

33
00:05:33.834 --> 00:05:36.170
Move it up! Come on!

34
00:05:36.420 --> 00:05:39.631
Let's go!

35
00:05:41.341 --> 00:05:44.720
The Channel coast is socked in
with rain and fog.

36
00:05:44.970 --> 00:05:49.600
High winds on the drop zone.
No jump tonight.

37
00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:54.521
The invasion has been postponed.
We're on a 24-hour stand-down.

38
00:05:54.771 --> 00:05:58.609
- Drill sergeants. take charge.
- 1st Platoon...

39
00:05:58.859 --> 00:06:02.154
<i>Well. this is quite a surprise.</i>

40
00:06:02.404 --> 00:06:06.158
<i>Not particularly. It so happens
I rather expected it.</i>

41
00:06:06.408 --> 00:06:11.997
<i>Well. I can't see how you people
can pass up $80.000 for the cause.</i>

42
00:06:12.247 --> 00:06:13.999
<i>For whose cause?</i>

43
00:06:14.249 --> 00:06:20.839
<i>If you're so interested in serving
a cause. why don't you join the Army?</i>

44
00:06:21.715 --> 00:06:23.967
<i>-I'm 4-F.
-You look 1-A to me.</i>

45
00:06:24.218 --> 00:06:28.305
<i>You don't look so bad yourself.</i>

46
00:06:29.431 --> 00:06:31.767
<i>Well. it's my arteries.</i>

47
00:06:32.017 --> 00:06:35.938
<i>Should you be giving blood?</i>

48
00:06:41.443 --> 00:06:45.239
I think it's clearing up.

49
00:06:46.490 --> 00:06:49.201
Think it's clearing up?

50
00:06:49.451 --> 00:06:51.745
Nope.

51
00:06:51.995 --> 00:06:55.707
I think it's clearing up.

52
00:06:56.375 --> 00:07:01.922
- How are your men?
- They'll be fine.

53
00:07:05.926 --> 00:07:11.139
Five o'clock in New York.
Four o'clock in Chicago.

54
00:07:11.390 --> 00:07:15.686
- Happy hour. huh?
- Yeah. happy hour.

55
00:07:15.936 --> 00:07:22.234
A couple of drinks. Maybe
an early dinner before the theater.

56
00:07:26.864 --> 00:07:31.743
Civilized place for civilized men.

57
00:07:34.454 --> 00:07:37.416
Should have been born earlier. Nix.

58
00:07:37.666 --> 00:07:41.795
What. and give up all this?

59
00:07:54.224 --> 00:07:57.144
We'll go to Chicago.
I'll take you there.

60
00:07:57.394 --> 00:07:59.771
Yeah.

61
00:08:00.022 --> 00:08:03.150
We'll see.

62
00:08:10.282 --> 00:08:15.537
- Actually. you know who's from there?
- Who? Oh. him.

63
00:08:15.787 --> 00:08:21.793
712 days with that son of a bitch
and here we are.

64
00:08:45.859 --> 00:08:51.907
You people are at the position
of attention!

65
00:08:57.412 --> 00:09:01.834
Pvt. Perconte. did you blouse
your trousers like a paratrooper?

66
00:09:02.084 --> 00:09:05.212
- No. sir.
- Then explain the creases.

67
00:09:05.462 --> 00:09:08.465
- No excuse. sir.
- Volunteering is one thing.

68
00:09:08.715 --> 00:09:11.635
You've got a long way
to prove you belong.

69
00:09:11.885 --> 00:09:14.513
Your weekend pass is revoked.

70
00:09:14.763 --> 00:09:18.183
- Name.
- Luz. George.

71
00:09:18.433 --> 00:09:23.689
Dirt in the rear sight aperture.
Pass revoked.

72
00:09:34.074 --> 00:09:36.285
When did you sew on the chevron?

73
00:09:36.535 --> 00:09:38.078
Yesterday. sir.

74
00:09:38.328 --> 00:09:40.747
Long enough to notice this. Revoked.

75
00:09:40.998 --> 00:09:43.959
Sir.

76
00:09:44.209 --> 00:09:46.503
- Name.
- Malarkey. Donald G.

77
00:09:46.753 --> 00:09:51.592
- Isn't "malarkey" slang for bullshit?
- Yes. sir.

78
00:09:51.842 --> 00:09:57.181
Rust on the butt plate hinge spring.
Pvt. Bullshit. Revoked.

79
00:09:57.431 --> 00:10:02.227
- Name.
- Liebgott. Joseph D.. sir.

80
00:10:02.811 --> 00:10:06.523
Rusty bayonet. Liebgott.
You wanna kill Germans?

81
00:10:06.773 --> 00:10:10.652
- Yes. sir.
- Not with this.

82
00:10:10.903 --> 00:10:14.281
I wouldn't take this rusty piece
of shit to war...

83
00:10:14.531 --> 00:10:17.618
...and I will not take you
in your condition.

84
00:10:17.868 --> 00:10:21.497
Thanks to these men
and their infractions. every man...

85
00:10:21.747 --> 00:10:27.461
...who had a weekend pass
has lost it.

86
00:10:27.669 --> 00:10:32.841
Change into your PT gear.
We're running Currahee.

87
00:10:33.800 --> 00:10:38.931
2nd Platoon. fall out.
We have two minutes.

88
00:10:42.643 --> 00:10:45.312
I ain't going up that hill.

89
00:10:45.562 --> 00:10:49.274
Perconte. what are you thinking of.
blousing your pants?

90
00:10:49.525 --> 00:10:54.238
- Shut up. He gigged everybody.
- Don't give him no excuses.

91
00:10:54.488 --> 00:10:59.451
Excuses? Look at these trousers and
tell me if there's a crease on them.

92
00:10:59.701 --> 00:11:04.039
Let's go. On the road.
in PT formation. Let's move.

93
00:11:04.289 --> 00:11:08.836
Perconte. Let's go. Perconte.

94
00:11:10.337 --> 00:11:15.175
Pvt. White. why are you not
in your PT gear?

95
00:11:18.053 --> 00:11:22.391
I asked you a question. private.

96
00:11:37.823 --> 00:11:42.369
Easy Company. While you run.
we'll take your dames to the movies.

97
00:11:42.619 --> 00:11:47.749
Good. they need some female company.

98
00:11:50.961 --> 00:11:53.255
- Where do we run?
- Currahee!

99
00:11:53.505 --> 00:11:56.049
<i>- What's Currahee mean?
- We stand alone!</i>

100
00:11:56.300 --> 00:11:59.970
- How far up? How far down?
- Three miles up. three down!

101
00:12:00.220 --> 00:12:02.764
- What company is this?
- Easy Company!

102
00:12:03.015 --> 00:12:05.267
- And what do we do?
- Stand alone!

103
00:12:05.517 --> 00:12:11.773
Do not help that man!
Do not help that man! Do not stop!

104
00:12:12.024 --> 00:12:15.861
You have 13 minutes to get
to the top of this mountain...

105
00:12:16.111 --> 00:12:23.410
...if you want to serve
in the paratroopers. Hi-yo. Silver!

106
00:12:46.892 --> 00:12:48.644
Come on. You can make it.

107
00:12:48.894 --> 00:12:52.439
Come on. Alley. Come on. Guarnere.
You got it! Come on!

108
00:12:52.689 --> 00:12:55.984
Never thought I'd see the day.
Private Wynn.

109
00:12:56.235 --> 00:12:59.071
We are coming on 23 minutes.

110
00:12:59.321 --> 00:13:02.616
That may be good enough
for the rest of the 506...

111
00:13:02.866 --> 00:13:08.247
...but that is not good
enough for Easy Company!

112
00:13:16.588 --> 00:13:20.217
We can do this! Come on!

113
00:13:20.259 --> 00:13:23.220
Come on.

114
00:13:23.762 --> 00:13:26.932
Come on.

115
00:13:47.536 --> 00:13:49.580
I'm gonna say something.

116
00:13:49.830 --> 00:13:52.875
To who?

117
00:13:54.501 --> 00:13:56.587
Lt. Winters.

118
00:13:56.837 --> 00:14:00.007
- What is it?
- Permission to speak. sir.

119
00:14:00.257 --> 00:14:04.094
- Permission granted.
- Sir. we've got nine companies. sir.

120
00:14:04.344 --> 00:14:06.263
We do.

121
00:14:06.513 --> 00:14:12.603
Why are we the only one marching every
Friday. 12 miles. in the pitch dark?

122
00:14:12.853 --> 00:14:19.902
- Why do you think. Pvt. Randleman?
- Lt. Sobel hates us. sir.

123
00:14:22.446 --> 00:14:26.992
Lt. Sobel does not hate Easy Company.
Pvt. Randleman.

124
00:14:27.242 --> 00:14:29.328
He just hates you.

125
00:14:29.578 --> 00:14:33.123
Thank you. sir.

126
00:14:33.957 --> 00:14:37.336
- He hates him back.
- He hates you too. Muck.

127
00:14:37.586 --> 00:14:40.964
Lt. Winters. I want canteens out.
caps unscrewed.

128
00:14:41.215 --> 00:14:43.133
Canteens out and open.

129
00:14:43.383 --> 00:14:46.386
They will pour the contents
onto the ground.

130
00:14:46.637 --> 00:14:48.847
You will upend your canteen.

131
00:14:49.097 --> 00:14:53.519
- Now. lieutenant.
- Pour them!

132
00:14:57.731 --> 00:14:59.483
Who is this?

133
00:14:59.733 --> 00:15:03.111
Christenson! Why is there
no water in your canteen?

134
00:15:03.362 --> 00:15:05.280
You drank from your canteen?

135
00:15:05.531 --> 00:15:07.115
- Lt. Winters!
- Yes. sir.

136
00:15:07.366 --> 00:15:11.870
Was this man ordered
to not drink from his canteen?

137
00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:15.290
- He was. sir.
- You disobeyed a direct order.

138
00:15:15.541 --> 00:15:20.254
You will fill your canteen
and repeat all 12 miles of the march.

139
00:15:20.504 --> 00:15:24.633
- Yes. sir.
- Fall out!

140
00:15:31.431 --> 00:15:34.434
What are you doing
with my company?

141
00:15:34.685 --> 00:15:38.438
You're late and you allow troopers
to disobey orders?

142
00:15:38.689 --> 00:15:41.149
No excuse. sir.

143
00:15:41.400 --> 00:15:45.362
You're making me look bad.
This is not Dog Company.

144
00:15:45.612 --> 00:15:50.492
This is not Fox Company.
This is Easy Company.

145
00:15:50.742 --> 00:15:56.665
Under my command. this will be
the first and finest company.

146
00:15:57.040 --> 00:15:59.835
I want the names of six men...

147
00:16:00.085 --> 00:16:04.673
...their infractions and your
disciplinary recommendations by 0130.

148
00:16:04.923 --> 00:16:07.176
Is that clear?

149
00:16:07.426 --> 00:16:09.970
What infractions. sir?

150
00:16:10.220 --> 00:16:13.891
Find some.

151
00:16:16.310 --> 00:16:18.061
So. what did you do?

152
00:16:18.312 --> 00:16:21.064
Picked six men
and gave them latrine duty.

153
00:16:21.315 --> 00:16:22.399
The lucky six?

154
00:16:22.649 --> 00:16:28.989
McDonald. Toye. Perconte.
Lipton. Muck and Guarnere.

155
00:16:29.239 --> 00:16:32.534
- Why them?
- It was their turn.

156
00:16:32.784 --> 00:16:34.536
Sobel's a genius.

157
00:16:34.786 --> 00:16:38.415
I had a headmaster like him
in school. I know the type.

158
00:16:38.665 --> 00:16:42.419
Lewis. Michelangelo's a genius.
Beethoven's a genius.

159
00:16:42.669 --> 00:16:46.089
You know a man who wouldn't
double-time Currahee...

160
00:16:46.340 --> 00:16:49.801
...just to piss in that guy's
morning coffee?

161
00:16:50.052 --> 00:16:51.512
Let's go. let's go.

162
00:16:51.762 --> 00:16:54.056
- Go!
- 1000. 2000. 3000. 4000...

163
00:16:54.306 --> 00:16:55.724
Stand in the door.

164
00:16:55.974 --> 00:16:57.726
- Go!
- 1000. 2000...

165
00:16:57.976 --> 00:17:00.646
You just broke both your legs. Gordon.

166
00:17:00.896 --> 00:17:04.566
- Are you trying to get killed?
- No. sir!

167
00:17:04.816 --> 00:17:08.612
Stand in the door.

168
00:17:20.457 --> 00:17:23.377
Shit.

169
00:17:27.881 --> 00:17:32.469
To the wall! Over as a team.
Come on. against the wall!

170
00:17:32.719 --> 00:17:34.847
Jesus. what the hell is this?

171
00:17:35.097 --> 00:17:38.892
That's pig guts. boy.

172
00:17:40.936 --> 00:17:44.481
Goddamn it.

173
00:17:44.773 --> 00:17:47.526
- Why are you here?
- To be in the Airborne.

174
00:17:47.776 --> 00:17:51.113
- I don't believe you. Why?
- To be in the Airborne.

175
00:17:51.363 --> 00:17:55.993
You have 50 minutes to the top and
back. and I will be watching you.

176
00:17:56.243 --> 00:18:00.289
What are you waiting for?

177
00:18:39.536 --> 00:18:44.124
Easy Company has the best performance
record in the 2nd Battalion.

178
00:18:44.374 --> 00:18:48.212
I believe every bit of that
is thanks to you.

179
00:18:48.462 --> 00:18:52.508
- Congratulations. Captain Sobel.
- Thank you. sir.

180
00:18:52.758 --> 00:18:56.678
Isn't that Lt. Winters leading
Easy Company in PT?

181
00:18:56.929 --> 00:18:58.347
Yes. sir.

182
00:18:58.597 --> 00:19:02.434
He's a good man. I was planning
on giving him these today.

183
00:19:02.684 --> 00:19:08.398
Why don't you do it?
He'd be proud to get them from you.

184
00:19:11.944 --> 00:19:15.864
Pornography. contraband.

185
00:19:17.699 --> 00:19:21.703
Non-regulation clothing. contraband.

186
00:19:21.954 --> 00:19:26.416
This man had 200 prophylactic kits
in his footlocker.

187
00:19:26.667 --> 00:19:31.463
How in the name of God was he gonna
have the strength to fight the war?

188
00:19:31.713 --> 00:19:38.512
How is it Pvt. Tipper has spare time
for so much correspondence?

189
00:19:38.762 --> 00:19:43.559
Captain. are personal letters
to be considered contraband?

190
00:19:43.809 --> 00:19:51.275
These men aren't paratroopers yet.
They have no personal property.

191
00:19:52.776 --> 00:19:55.153
What is this?

192
00:19:55.404 --> 00:19:57.531
Anybody.

193
00:19:57.781 --> 00:19:59.283
It's a can of peaches.

194
00:19:59.533 --> 00:20:03.412
Lt. Nixon thinks this
is a can of peaches.

195
00:20:03.662 --> 00:20:06.957
That is incorrect.
Your weekend pass is cancelled.

196
00:20:07.207 --> 00:20:11.670
This is United States Army property...

197
00:20:11.920 --> 00:20:16.383
...which was taken without
authorization from my mess facility.

198
00:20:16.633 --> 00:20:21.305
And I will not tolerate thievery
in my unit. Whose footlocker is this?

199
00:20:21.555 --> 00:20:23.932
Private Parks'. sir.

200
00:20:24.183 --> 00:20:27.186
Get rid of him.

201
00:20:27.436 --> 00:20:32.983
All weekend passes are cancelled.
officers included.

202
00:20:33.233 --> 00:20:36.320
Carry on.

203
00:20:38.947 --> 00:20:42.201
Lt. Winters.

204
00:20:48.624 --> 00:20:52.127
Colonel Sink has seen fit
to promote you.

205
00:20:52.377 --> 00:20:56.507
As first lieutenant. you'll serve
as my executive officer.

206
00:20:56.757 --> 00:20:59.384
- Congratulations.
- Thank you. sir.

207
00:20:59.635 --> 00:21:06.391
And as a test of your organizational
skills and command potential...

208
00:21:06.642 --> 00:21:11.605
...I am designating you
mess officer for 14 days.

209
00:21:11.855 --> 00:21:14.525
Report to the mess kitchen
at 0515 hours.

210
00:21:14.775 --> 00:21:18.487
Company breakfast
to be served at 0600.

211
00:21:18.737 --> 00:21:21.448
Yes. sir.

212
00:21:21.698 --> 00:21:24.993
And. Dick. there's rain
forecast tomorrow.

213
00:21:25.244 --> 00:21:32.417
The company will have a light afternoon
of lecture and classroom instruction.

214
00:21:32.668 --> 00:21:37.881
A special meal before their afternoon
off would be a welcome change of pace.

215
00:21:38.131 --> 00:21:41.552
- Would you agree?
- Yes. sir.

216
00:21:41.802 --> 00:21:45.180
I like spaghetti.

217
00:21:52.938 --> 00:21:54.857
Hold on. more coming.

218
00:21:55.107 --> 00:21:59.653
These guys are packing it away.

219
00:22:08.412 --> 00:22:11.790
It's orange. Spaghetti ain't
supposed to be orange.

220
00:22:12.040 --> 00:22:15.586
This ain't spaghetti.
It's Army noodles with ketchup.

221
00:22:15.836 --> 00:22:17.379
You ain't gotta eat it.

222
00:22:17.629 --> 00:22:22.134
As an Italian. you know calling
this spaghetti is a mortal sin.

223
00:22:22.384 --> 00:22:24.178
- I'll eat it.
- I'm eating!

224
00:22:24.428 --> 00:22:27.806
Get out of here!

225
00:22:27.890 --> 00:22:29.933
Orders changed! Get up!

226
00:22:30.184 --> 00:22:37.482
Lectures are cancelled! Easy Company
is running up Currahee! Move!

227
00:22:38.775 --> 00:22:41.987
Three miles up. three miles down.

228
00:22:42.237 --> 00:22:44.865
Hi-yo. Silver!

229
00:22:45.115 --> 00:22:48.994
Let's go! Let's go!

230
00:22:51.538 --> 00:22:56.043
You're a washout. Pvt. Hoobler.
You should pack up and go home!

231
00:22:56.293 --> 00:23:01.715
Looks like Gordon's done. Finished?
You do not deserve to get your wings.

232
00:23:01.965 --> 00:23:04.551
Pvt. Randleman. you look tired.

233
00:23:04.801 --> 00:23:07.930
There's an ambulance waiting for you.

234
00:23:08.180 --> 00:23:11.433
It can all be over. right now.
No more pain...

235
00:23:11.683 --> 00:23:16.855
...no more Currahee.
no more Captain Sobel.

236
00:23:56.603 --> 00:24:00.357
- Are we ready to be Army paratroopers?
- Yes. sergeant!

237
00:24:00.607 --> 00:24:01.900
I hope so.

238
00:24:02.150 --> 00:24:06.905
This will be the first of five exits
from a C-47 aircraft set for today.

239
00:24:07.155 --> 00:24:09.241
Get ready!

240
00:24:09.491 --> 00:24:12.161
Stand up! Hook up!

241
00:24:12.411 --> 00:24:17.541
<i>Upon completion of your final jump.
you'll be certified paratroopers.</i>

242
00:24:17.791 --> 00:24:20.878
Check equipment!

243
00:24:21.461 --> 00:24:24.006
Sound off for equipment check!

244
00:24:24.256 --> 00:24:25.757
Nine okay!

245
00:24:26.008 --> 00:24:28.635
Eight okay! Seven okay!

246
00:24:28.886 --> 00:24:30.804
Six okay!

247
00:24:31.054 --> 00:24:33.682
Five okay! Four okay!

248
00:24:33.932 --> 00:24:36.935
Three okay! Two okay! One okay!

249
00:24:37.186 --> 00:24:42.691
There'll be many men jumping today.
hopefully under deployed canopies.

250
00:24:42.941 --> 00:24:46.904
Stand in the door!

251
00:24:47.446 --> 00:24:51.617
I guarantee you're gonna love it.
lieutenant! Go! Go!

252
00:24:51.867 --> 00:24:57.831
Jumping from 1000 feet AGL.
in sticks of 12 jumpers per aircraft.

253
00:24:58.081 --> 00:25:01.210
You just have to remember
what you were taught.

254
00:25:01.460 --> 00:25:04.546
I guarantee gravity will
take care of the rest.

255
00:25:04.796 --> 00:25:08.509
Go! Go! Go!

256
00:25:49.007 --> 00:25:51.385
Damn it.

257
00:25:51.635 --> 00:25:58.433
Gentlemen. rest assured. any refusals
in the aircraft or at the door...

258
00:25:58.684 --> 00:26:02.980
...and I guarantee you will be
out of the Airborne.

259
00:26:03.230 --> 00:26:07.150
Four okay! Three okay!
Two okay! One okay!

260
00:26:07.401 --> 00:26:10.946
Stand in the door!

261
00:26:11.530 --> 00:26:14.658
Now!

262
00:26:24.126 --> 00:26:27.546
1000. 2000. 3000. 4000. 5000...

263
00:26:27.796 --> 00:26:31.466
...6000. 7000. 8000. 9000.

264
00:26:31.717 --> 00:26:34.595
Yeah!

265
00:26:35.220 --> 00:26:39.057
Hi-yo. Silver!

266
00:26:42.978 --> 00:26:47.566
If you had style like me. somebody
might mistake you for somebody.

267
00:26:47.816 --> 00:26:51.528
You mean like your fucking sergeant?

268
00:26:51.778 --> 00:26:55.365
I'm just kidding.

269
00:26:56.158 --> 00:26:58.660
- Congratulations. Martin.
- Cpl. Toye.

270
00:26:58.911 --> 00:27:02.623
There will be no leaning
in my company.

271
00:27:02.873 --> 00:27:05.542
Are those dusty jump wings?

272
00:27:05.792 --> 00:27:09.588
How will you slay the Huns
with dust on your jump wings?

273
00:27:09.838 --> 00:27:13.926
Luz. just give me a drink.

274
00:27:14.092 --> 00:27:15.886
Hell of an idea. Joe.

275
00:27:16.136 --> 00:27:18.597
There you go.

276
00:27:18.847 --> 00:27:22.643
Three miles up. three miles down.

277
00:27:22.893 --> 00:27:26.313
Ten-hut!

278
00:27:33.946 --> 00:27:37.449
Well. at ease. paratroopers.

279
00:27:37.699 --> 00:27:40.828
- Good evening. Easy Company.
- Evening. sir!

280
00:27:41.078 --> 00:27:44.957
Parachute Infantry is a new concept
in military history.

281
00:27:45.207 --> 00:27:48.752
But the 506 will forge
that new concept into victory.

282
00:27:49.002 --> 00:27:50.337
Yes. sir!

283
00:27:50.587 --> 00:27:54.216
I want you to know I'm damn proud
of every one of you.

284
00:27:54.466 --> 00:27:57.094
Now. you deserve this party.

285
00:27:57.344 --> 00:27:59.304
- Thanks. Sgt. Grant.
- Sir.

286
00:27:59.555 --> 00:28:03.058
So I want you to have fun.
and remember our motto:

287
00:28:03.308 --> 00:28:07.604
- Currahee!
- Currahee!

288
00:28:32.963 --> 00:28:34.381
Petty!

289
00:28:34.631 --> 00:28:36.633
Map! Come on!

290
00:28:36.884 --> 00:28:40.345
Oh. Christ.

291
00:28:51.356 --> 00:28:55.694
We're in the wrong position.

292
00:28:56.195 --> 00:29:00.157
- We're in the wrong position.
- We're in position for ambush.

293
00:29:00.407 --> 00:29:03.327
Let the enemy come
into our killing zone.

294
00:29:03.577 --> 00:29:06.538
They're right out there.
Let's get them.

295
00:29:06.788 --> 00:29:13.086
- Sir. we have perfect cover here.
- Lieutenant. deploy your troops.

296
00:29:13.378 --> 00:29:16.256
2nd Platoon. move out.

297
00:29:16.507 --> 00:29:20.385
- What?
- Tactical column.

298
00:29:38.195 --> 00:29:42.407
You've just been killed.
along with 95% of your company.

299
00:29:42.658 --> 00:29:44.660
Your outfit?

300
00:29:44.910 --> 00:29:49.289
Easy Company.
2nd Battalion. 506.

301
00:29:51.250 --> 00:29:56.421
Leave three wounded men on the ground
and report back to the assembly area.

302
00:29:56.672 --> 00:30:00.092
Goddamn it.

303
00:30:03.262 --> 00:30:07.057
You. You. You.

304
00:30:08.642 --> 00:30:10.227
What are you gonna do?

305
00:30:10.477 --> 00:30:13.981
Nothing. just keep training the men.

306
00:30:14.231 --> 00:30:17.234
Am I interrupting?

307
00:30:17.484 --> 00:30:19.278
No. no.

308
00:30:19.528 --> 00:30:23.448
Lt. Lewis Nixon. Lt. Harry Welsh.
just in from the 82nd.

309
00:30:23.699 --> 00:30:27.661
- Congratulations on the promotion.
- Lf you wanna call it that.

310
00:30:27.911 --> 00:30:32.499
You'll learn him pretty quickly.
No flaws. vices or sense of humor.

311
00:30:32.749 --> 00:30:36.086
Just like your chums
up at Battalion Staff?

312
00:30:36.336 --> 00:30:39.798
- What's up?
- I'm hearing a lot of rumblings.

313
00:30:40.048 --> 00:30:43.135
Sobel? We were just
talking about that.

314
00:30:43.385 --> 00:30:46.180
So he gets a little jumpy
in the field.

315
00:30:46.430 --> 00:30:50.058
- He gets jumpy and you get killed.
- That's nice.

316
00:30:50.309 --> 00:30:53.937
Listen. if we discuss it.
it should be among ourselves.

317
00:30:54.188 --> 00:30:57.399
Absolutely.

318
00:31:03.447 --> 00:31:06.992
- 2nd Platoon ready?
- Ready. sir.

319
00:31:07.242 --> 00:31:10.454
Then get them in formation.
We're moving out.

320
00:31:10.704 --> 00:31:13.749
Yes. sir.

321
00:31:37.356 --> 00:31:41.485
Goddamn. you gotta admit.
He's got no chance.

322
00:31:41.735 --> 00:31:45.447
Either the Krauts will get him.
or one of us.

323
00:31:45.697 --> 00:31:47.407
Who? Sobel?

324
00:31:47.658 --> 00:31:49.451
He screwed up one maneuver.

325
00:31:49.701 --> 00:31:52.079
I'm always fumbling with grenades.

326
00:31:52.329 --> 00:31:55.249
It would be easy if one
went off by accident.

327
00:31:55.499 --> 00:31:59.127
They must have put him
in charge for a reason.

328
00:31:59.378 --> 00:32:04.675
Because the Army wouldn't
make a mistake. right. Shift?

329
00:32:17.396 --> 00:32:20.065
- Going my way?
- Where the train takes me.

330
00:32:20.315 --> 00:32:22.442
- Where's that?
- I haven't a clue.

331
00:32:22.693 --> 00:32:26.989
Yeah. come on. Take a guess.
Atlantic. Pacific. Atlantic?

332
00:32:27.239 --> 00:32:30.409
I'm not the intelligence officer.

333
00:32:30.659 --> 00:32:34.413
As such. I know. but if I told you.
I'd have to kill you.

334
00:32:34.663 --> 00:32:38.083
So don't tell me.

335
00:32:39.501 --> 00:32:44.882
New York City. Troop ship. England.

336
00:32:46.216 --> 00:32:49.136
We're invading Europe. my friend.

337
00:32:49.386 --> 00:32:52.764
Fortress Europa.

338
00:32:52.890 --> 00:32:56.310
Since when do I drink?

339
00:32:56.560 --> 00:33:01.732
If I thought you'd drink.
I wouldn't offer it to you.

340
00:33:01.982 --> 00:33:07.237
Nix. what are you gonna do
when you get into combat?

341
00:33:08.155 --> 00:33:12.159
Oh. I have every confidence
in my scrounging abilities.

342
00:33:12.409 --> 00:33:18.373
And I have a case of Vat 69
hidden in your footlocker.

343
00:33:20.667 --> 00:33:24.546
- Really?
- Oh. yeah.

344
00:33:24.713 --> 00:33:27.799
Morning.

345
00:33:28.091 --> 00:33:32.721
This could turn into a real nice trip.

346
00:33:46.860 --> 00:33:48.946
<i>Dear Sir or Madam:</i>

347
00:33:49.196 --> 00:33:54.535
<i>Soon your son will drop from the sky
to engage and defeat the enemy.</i>

348
00:33:54.785 --> 00:34:00.374
<i>Your letters of love and encouragement
will arm him with a fighting heart.</i>

349
00:34:00.624 --> 00:34:06.421
<i>With that. he cannot fail but will win
glory for himself. make you proud...</i>

350
00:34:06.672 --> 00:34:10.926
<i>... and his country grateful
for his service in its hour of need.</i>

351
00:34:11.176 --> 00:34:16.515
<i>Signed Herbert M. Sobel.
Captain. Commanding.</i>

352
00:34:27.693 --> 00:34:32.447
Right now. some lucky bastard's
headed for the South Pacific.

353
00:34:32.698 --> 00:34:35.701
He'll get billeted
on some tropical island.

354
00:34:35.951 --> 00:34:39.037
Sitting under a tree
with naked native girls...

355
00:34:39.288 --> 00:34:43.625
...helping him cut up coconuts
so he can hand-feed the flamingos.

356
00:34:43.876 --> 00:34:48.130
- Flamingos are mean. They bite.
- So do the naked native girls.

357
00:34:48.380 --> 00:34:49.590
With any luck.

358
00:34:49.840 --> 00:34:52.134
Guys. I'm glad I'm going to Europe.

359
00:34:52.384 --> 00:34:55.012
Hitler gets this
across the windpipe.

360
00:34:55.262 --> 00:34:58.515
Roosevelt changes Thanksgiving
to Joe Toye Day...

361
00:34:58.765 --> 00:35:02.561
...and pays me $ 10.000 a year
for the rest of my life.

362
00:35:02.811 --> 00:35:06.315
What if they send us to North Africa?

363
00:35:06.565 --> 00:35:10.569
- My brother's there. He says it's hot.
- It's hot in Africa?

364
00:35:10.819 --> 00:35:14.072
Shut up.
Point is. it don't matter where we go.

365
00:35:14.323 --> 00:35:19.995
Once we get into combat. you trust
only yourself and the man next to you.

366
00:35:20.245 --> 00:35:22.623
- Long as he's a paratrooper.
- Yeah?

367
00:35:22.873 --> 00:35:25.959
What if that paratrooper
turns out to be Sobel?

368
00:35:26.210 --> 00:35:29.671
If I'm next to Sobel.
I'm moving down the line.

369
00:35:29.922 --> 00:35:33.550
Hook up with another officer.
like Heyliger or Winters.

370
00:35:33.800 --> 00:35:39.890
I like Winters. But when bullets fly.
I don't want a Quaker fighting for me.

371
00:35:40.140 --> 00:35:43.185
- How do you know that?
- He ain't Catholic.

372
00:35:43.435 --> 00:35:47.814
- Neither's Sobel.
- That prick's a son of Abraham.

373
00:35:48.065 --> 00:35:50.692
- He's what?
- He's a Jew.

374
00:35:50.943 --> 00:35:54.029
Fuck.

375
00:35:54.696 --> 00:35:58.116
- I'm a Jew.
- Congratulations.

376
00:35:58.367 --> 00:36:02.454
Get your nose out of my face.

377
00:36:07.584 --> 00:36:09.378
What's all that about?

378
00:36:09.628 --> 00:36:11.588
Gonorrhea called Sobel a Jew.

379
00:36:11.839 --> 00:36:15.467
Liebgott took offense
because he's a Jew too.

380
00:36:15.717 --> 00:36:21.014
Fighting over Sobel. That's smart.

381
00:36:36.780 --> 00:36:40.033
Attack!

382
00:36:41.660 --> 00:36:44.246
No! You wanna kill him!

383
00:36:44.496 --> 00:36:47.541
Parry right! Parry left!
Front!

384
00:36:47.791 --> 00:36:48.917
Recover.

385
00:36:49.168 --> 00:36:50.294
Okay.

386
00:36:50.544 --> 00:36:56.675
We talked about magnetic declination
and the left-add. right-subtract rule.

387
00:36:56.925 --> 00:36:58.594
Today we'll use it.

388
00:36:58.844 --> 00:37:01.722
There are two basic
fighting positions.

389
00:37:01.972 --> 00:37:04.474
The first is a prepared position.

390
00:37:04.725 --> 00:37:10.230
This position's advantages are that
it gives you cover and concealment.

391
00:37:10.480 --> 00:37:14.193
Commence fire!

392
00:37:16.653 --> 00:37:19.239
We'll maneuver through these trees.

393
00:37:19.490 --> 00:37:24.328
At the same time. our 2nd Platoon.
in this case. moves over here.

394
00:37:24.578 --> 00:37:29.416
He'll then kill or capture
that German.

395
00:37:52.898 --> 00:37:56.151
Sobel's late.

396
00:38:06.620 --> 00:38:10.499
Why is there a fence here?

397
00:38:11.041 --> 00:38:13.585
There should be no fence here.
Tipper!

398
00:38:13.836 --> 00:38:17.589
Give me the map.

399
00:38:18.340 --> 00:38:21.593
Perconte. Luz.
Get the men. Get them ba...

400
00:38:21.844 --> 00:38:28.559
- Take cover behind those trees.
- All right. Let's go. Move it out.

401
00:38:30.269 --> 00:38:33.063
There should...
There should be no fence.

402
00:38:33.313 --> 00:38:35.607
We could go over it. sir.

403
00:38:35.858 --> 00:38:39.236
Really? That's not the point.
Where the goddamn...?

404
00:38:39.486 --> 00:38:42.948
Where the goddamn hell are we?

405
00:38:43.198 --> 00:38:44.283
- Perconte.
- Yeah?

406
00:38:44.533 --> 00:38:46.743
- Sobel's lost again. right?
- Yeah.

407
00:38:46.994 --> 00:38:50.706
- Fucking Christ.
- Hey. Luz?

408
00:38:52.040 --> 00:38:54.668
Can you do Major Horton?

409
00:38:54.918 --> 00:38:58.630
Does a wild bear crap
in the woods. son?

410
00:38:58.881 --> 00:39:02.509
Maybe the major can goose
this schmuck. Get us moving?

411
00:39:02.759 --> 00:39:04.970
- No way. I'm not gonna...
- Oh. yes.

412
00:39:05.220 --> 00:39:07.598
Luz. you gotta. Come on.

413
00:39:07.848 --> 00:39:11.602
All right. just this once.

414
00:39:14.479 --> 00:39:18.734
356833.
Isn't that the intersection?

415
00:39:18.984 --> 00:39:22.237
No. sir. it's here.
You're a full grid off.

416
00:39:22.488 --> 00:39:24.114
Goddamn it.

417
00:39:24.364 --> 00:39:29.453
- Is there a problem. Captain Sobel?
- Who said that? Who broke silence?

418
00:39:29.703 --> 00:39:33.999
I think it's Major Horton. sir.

419
00:39:34.333 --> 00:39:37.503
Major Horton? What. is he...?
Did he join us?

420
00:39:37.753 --> 00:39:40.339
Maybe he's moving
between the platoons.

421
00:39:40.589 --> 00:39:46.303
What is the goddamn holdup.
Mr. Sobel?!

422
00:39:46.553 --> 00:39:50.140
A fence. sir. a...
God!

423
00:39:50.390 --> 00:39:54.895
- A barbed-wire fence.
- Oh. that dog just ain't gonna hunt.

424
00:39:55.145 --> 00:39:56.480
Shut up!

425
00:39:56.730 --> 00:40:02.569
Now. you cut that fence and get this
goddamn platoon on the move!

426
00:40:02.820 --> 00:40:06.156
Yes. sir!

427
00:40:06.698 --> 00:40:10.410
- Where are my wire cutters?
- Sir.

428
00:40:11.078 --> 00:40:15.249
- We have to move.
- Without Sobel and 1st Platoon?

429
00:40:15.499 --> 00:40:18.085
It's a T-intersection. We improvise.

430
00:40:18.335 --> 00:40:22.214
Lay down fire to cut the road
in all directions.

431
00:40:22.464 --> 00:40:27.177
Go right with 1st Squad. Tell 2nd
to go left. I'll be center with 3rd.

432
00:40:27.427 --> 00:40:31.139
- Go.
- Yes. sir.

433
00:40:51.702 --> 00:40:54.955
Dearie me.

434
00:41:04.047 --> 00:41:07.551
Bloody hell.

435
00:41:25.527 --> 00:41:31.033
You've done it now. Yanks.
You've captured me.

436
00:41:32.868 --> 00:41:38.415
Hi-yo. Silver!

437
00:41:39.458 --> 00:41:41.752
Would that be the enemy?

438
00:41:42.002 --> 00:41:46.048
As a matter of fact. yes.

439
00:41:51.803 --> 00:41:56.433
Good work. 2nd Platoon.
We took the objective.

440
00:42:04.024 --> 00:42:06.985
Who was the idiot
who cut that man's fence?

441
00:42:07.236 --> 00:42:09.154
- I was ordered to.
- By who?

442
00:42:09.404 --> 00:42:11.490
- Maj. Horton. sir.
- Maj. Horton?

443
00:42:11.740 --> 00:42:13.951
- Yes.
- He told you to do that?

444
00:42:14.201 --> 00:42:18.080
- Yes. sir.
- He ordered you to cut the fence?

445
00:42:18.330 --> 00:42:19.998
Yes. he did.

446
00:42:20.249 --> 00:42:26.046
Major Horton is on leave in London.

447
00:42:26.463 --> 00:42:30.425
Get those cows out of here.

448
00:42:57.202 --> 00:43:00.581
Lt. Winters.

449
00:43:01.957 --> 00:43:06.503
With Capt. Sobel's compliments. sir.

450
00:43:07.296 --> 00:43:10.299
Lieutenant.

451
00:43:27.733 --> 00:43:34.072
- Oh. for crying out loud.
- Misspelled "court-martial".

452
00:43:37.534 --> 00:43:39.536
No. sir. I do not understand.

453
00:43:39.786 --> 00:43:43.165
Your orders were to inspect
latrines at 1000 hours.

454
00:43:43.415 --> 00:43:49.588
From 0930 to 0955. I was censoring
mail by order of Col. Strayer.

455
00:43:49.838 --> 00:43:52.674
At 1000 hours. I followed your orders.

456
00:43:52.925 --> 00:43:55.552
I changed that time to 0945.

457
00:43:55.802 --> 00:43:57.763
- No one told me.
- I telephoned.

458
00:43:58.013 --> 00:44:00.224
The family I'm with has no phone.

459
00:44:00.474 --> 00:44:03.185
- And sent a runner.
- No runner found me.

460
00:44:03.435 --> 00:44:06.980
When given a task to perform
by a ranking officer...

461
00:44:07.231 --> 00:44:11.693
...you should have delegated
latrine inspection to another officer.

462
00:44:11.944 --> 00:44:13.487
You failed to do so.

463
00:44:13.737 --> 00:44:19.451
Were I to let this go unpunished. what
kind of message is that to the men?

464
00:44:19.701 --> 00:44:23.622
- I performed my duty as I was ordered.
- And I disagree.

465
00:44:23.872 --> 00:44:27.835
So your options are
quite simple. lieutenant.

466
00:44:28.085 --> 00:44:32.506
Punishment will be denial
of a 48-hour pass for 60 days.

467
00:44:32.756 --> 00:44:37.135
Stand before me at attention.

468
00:44:38.095 --> 00:44:44.434
Or you may initiate an appeal
and request a trial by court-martial.

469
00:44:47.437 --> 00:44:52.526
You spend weekends on the base anyway.
Be a man. Take the punishment.

470
00:44:52.776 --> 00:44:56.738
May I borrow your pen. sir?

471
00:45:06.665 --> 00:45:10.085
My endorsement. sir.

472
00:45:10.127 --> 00:45:14.464
I request trial by court-martial.

473
00:45:23.473 --> 00:45:26.476
- We lost Winters to the mess.
- You're joking.

474
00:45:26.727 --> 00:45:31.648
Strayer did it while he figures out
the procedures for his court-martial.

475
00:45:31.899 --> 00:45:35.068
- Nixon better get him out.
- And if he don't?

476
00:45:35.319 --> 00:45:40.491
Winters scrambles eggs while
we make the big jump with Sobel.

477
00:45:40.741 --> 00:45:42.576
Not me.

478
00:45:42.826 --> 00:45:46.955
- We're going through with this. right?
- We gotta do something.

479
00:45:47.206 --> 00:45:49.750
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

480
00:45:50.000 --> 00:45:51.627
All right.

481
00:45:51.877 --> 00:45:54.796
Good.

482
00:45:54.963 --> 00:46:00.302
- Let's be clear of the consequences.
- I don't care about the consequences.

483
00:46:00.552 --> 00:46:05.098
We could be lined up
against a wall and shot.

484
00:46:05.349 --> 00:46:08.644
Now. I'm ready to face that.

485
00:46:08.894 --> 00:46:13.440
And every one of us had better be too.

486
00:46:16.735 --> 00:46:22.157
I will not follow that man
into combat.

487
00:46:23.534 --> 00:46:26.745
Me neither.

488
00:46:27.621 --> 00:46:30.123
All right.

489
00:46:30.374 --> 00:46:33.877
Then let's do it.

490
00:46:45.722 --> 00:46:48.725
"I hereby...

491
00:46:48.976 --> 00:46:51.854
...no longer...

492
00:46:52.104 --> 00:46:55.649
...wish to serve...

493
00:46:56.275 --> 00:47:00.362
...as a non-commissioned officer...

494
00:47:05.367 --> 00:47:08.871
...in Easy Company."

495
00:47:20.966 --> 00:47:25.721
All right. boys. Good luck.

496
00:47:29.099 --> 00:47:31.560
I ought to have you all shot!

497
00:47:31.810 --> 00:47:36.648
This is an act of mutiny while
we prepare for the invasion of Europe.

498
00:47:36.899 --> 00:47:38.942
- Sgt. Harris?
- Sir.

499
00:47:39.193 --> 00:47:40.944
Turn in your stripes.

500
00:47:41.195 --> 00:47:44.072
You are transferred
out of my regiment.

501
00:47:44.323 --> 00:47:47.451
- Sir.
- Get out.

502
00:47:47.701 --> 00:47:49.953
- Sgt. Ranney?
- Sir.

503
00:47:50.204 --> 00:47:53.373
You're lucky I'm only
busting you to private.

504
00:47:53.624 --> 00:47:57.336
All of you NCOs have disgraced
the 101st Airborne.

505
00:47:57.586 --> 00:48:02.216
You're lucky we're on the eve of
the largest action in war history...

506
00:48:02.466 --> 00:48:09.223
...which leaves me no choice
but to spare your lives.

507
00:48:09.848 --> 00:48:13.101
Now. get out of my office
and out of my sight.

508
00:48:13.352 --> 00:48:16.230
Get.

509
00:48:31.036 --> 00:48:35.582
Keep them coming. Thattaboy.
That's it.

510
00:49:06.572 --> 00:49:10.033
I can only speculate.
Most men would never do this.

511
00:49:10.284 --> 00:49:14.204
But I believe just a few
of the sergeants may have felt...

512
00:49:14.454 --> 00:49:19.001
...their loyalty lay more
to the platoon than to the company.

513
00:49:19.251 --> 00:49:23.630
And these few convinced the other
NCOs to turn in their stripes?

514
00:49:23.881 --> 00:49:27.050
As staff sergeants.
they have a great influence.

515
00:49:27.301 --> 00:49:32.681
But the rest are good men.
I can work with them.

516
00:49:37.686 --> 00:49:42.149
Winters' court-martial has been
an unpleasant distraction.

517
00:49:42.399 --> 00:49:44.776
Indeed it has. sir.

518
00:49:45.027 --> 00:49:49.740
However. your command of Easy
Company has been exemplary.

519
00:49:49.990 --> 00:49:52.117
Thank you. sir.

520
00:49:52.367 --> 00:49:57.247
In fact. except for the actions
of a few of your non-coms...

521
00:49:57.498 --> 00:50:01.877
...you fielded one of the finest
companies of soldiers I've seen.

522
00:50:02.127 --> 00:50:04.379
Yes. sir.

523
00:50:04.630 --> 00:50:09.426
Division has established a parachute
training school at Chilton Foliat.

524
00:50:09.676 --> 00:50:13.639
The idea is for non-infantry types...

525
00:50:13.889 --> 00:50:17.726
...vital to the invasion.
such as doctors and chaplains...

526
00:50:17.976 --> 00:50:21.021
...to take jump training there.

527
00:50:21.271 --> 00:50:28.028
I can't think of anyone more qualified
to command such a school than you.

528
00:50:29.321 --> 00:50:32.241
Sir?

529
00:50:34.076 --> 00:50:38.789
I'm reassigning you to Chilton Foliat.

530
00:50:45.629 --> 00:50:47.548
I'm losing Easy Company?

531
00:50:47.798 --> 00:50:52.427
The war effort needs you elsewhere.

532
00:50:56.682 --> 00:51:01.478
- Permission to speak. sir.
- Granted.

533
00:51:04.022 --> 00:51:06.608
Is...? Who will be replacing me?

534
00:51:06.859 --> 00:51:12.239
Lt. Meehan from Baker Company
is senior.

535
00:51:12.531 --> 00:51:18.328
Good luck at Chilton Foliat. Herbert.
Don't let us down. now.

536
00:51:23.125 --> 00:51:26.128
No. sir.

537
00:51:31.466 --> 00:51:34.678
Carry on.

538
00:52:26.355 --> 00:52:31.443
2nd Platoon. listen up. I want
the 1st Squad in A-side tents there.

539
00:52:31.693 --> 00:52:35.906
3rd Squad. second row...

540
00:52:48.335 --> 00:52:51.380
Holy shit!

541
00:52:51.630 --> 00:52:54.675
No. it's all right.
We're Tommies. not Boche.

542
00:52:54.925 --> 00:52:57.094
- Is all this real?
- Yeah. yeah.

543
00:52:57.344 --> 00:53:02.724
It's for you lads. so you can get your
mince pies on some Jerry clobber.

544
00:53:02.975 --> 00:53:05.727
- Lf you know what I mean.
- Not really.

545
00:53:05.978 --> 00:53:07.271
You got a Luger?

546
00:53:07.521 --> 00:53:12.234
- I'm dying to hold a real Luger.
- Yeah. go on. then.

547
00:53:12.484 --> 00:53:16.321
Quick butchers. yeah?

548
00:53:18.323 --> 00:53:21.285
- She's a doozy.
- That's pukka. isn't it?

549
00:53:21.535 --> 00:53:23.871
- What?
- Eh?

550
00:53:24.121 --> 00:53:25.706
Hey. Petty!

551
00:53:25.956 --> 00:53:28.750
Hey. mate?

552
00:53:29.001 --> 00:53:32.796
You're having a bath if you think
you're half-inching that.

553
00:53:33.046 --> 00:53:35.465
Oh. yeah. Sorry. Well. good luck.

554
00:53:35.716 --> 00:53:38.343
You too. mate.

555
00:53:38.594 --> 00:53:40.762
What's up. Hoobs?

556
00:53:41.013 --> 00:53:44.766
These men have been through
the Army's toughest training.

557
00:53:45.017 --> 00:53:49.563
Under the worst circumstances.
And they volunteered for it.

558
00:53:49.813 --> 00:53:52.316
I was just shooting craps with them...

559
00:53:52.566 --> 00:53:54.526
You know why they volunteered?

560
00:53:54.776 --> 00:54:00.032
So when things got bad. the man
next to them would be the best.

561
00:54:00.282 --> 00:54:05.204
- Not a draftee who'll get them killed.
- Are you mad because they like me?

562
00:54:05.454 --> 00:54:08.248
Because I'm getting
to know my soldiers?

563
00:54:08.499 --> 00:54:13.587
You've been with these guys two years?
I've been here for six days.

564
00:54:13.837 --> 00:54:16.840
- You were gambling.
- So? Soldiers do that.

565
00:54:17.090 --> 00:54:22.804
- I don't deserve a reprimand for it.
- What if you'd won?

566
00:54:22.804 --> 00:54:27.851
- What?
- What if you'd won?

567
00:54:31.021 --> 00:54:37.110
Never put yourself in a position
where you can take from these men.

568
00:54:40.239 --> 00:54:43.867
- Lt. Meehan?
- Enter.

569
00:54:44.827 --> 00:54:49.373
On the last training jump...
I had a compass.

570
00:54:49.623 --> 00:54:53.043
Close the flap.

571
00:54:53.418 --> 00:54:55.254
- Then we turned left.
- Yeah.

572
00:54:55.504 --> 00:54:59.383
Bearing 0-4-2. 12 minutes.

573
00:54:59.633 --> 00:55:02.177
- Then another left.
- Yes.

574
00:55:02.427 --> 00:55:05.764
Call it 3-5-8.

575
00:55:06.014 --> 00:55:08.392
For 10 1/2 minutes.

576
00:55:08.642 --> 00:55:11.979
- Green light. right over Ramsbury.
- Ramsbury.

577
00:55:12.229 --> 00:55:14.648
Every single time.

578
00:55:14.898 --> 00:55:20.529
Linear distance on the grid
of about...

579
00:55:20.988 --> 00:55:24.199
Okay. Ramsbury.

580
00:55:24.449 --> 00:55:27.536
Upottery.

581
00:55:33.542 --> 00:55:35.252
So...

582
00:55:35.502 --> 00:55:38.005
It's Normandy.

583
00:55:38.255 --> 00:55:41.008
Sainte-Marie-du-Mont.
Causeway number one.

584
00:55:41.258 --> 00:55:45.804
Causeway number two.
The ultimate field problem.

585
00:55:46.054 --> 00:55:50.851
The Douve River estuary divides two
beachheads. code name Utah. here...

586
00:55:51.101 --> 00:55:52.978
...and Omaha. here.

587
00:55:53.228 --> 00:55:58.567
Seaborne Infantry will hit these
beaches at a specified date and time.

588
00:55:58.817 --> 00:56:00.777
H-Hour. D-Day.

589
00:56:01.028 --> 00:56:04.990
Airborne's objective is to take
the town of Carentan...

590
00:56:05.240 --> 00:56:09.036
...linking Utah and Omaha
into a continuous beachhead.

591
00:56:09.286 --> 00:56:13.165
...linking Omaha and Utah
into one continuous beachhead.

592
00:56:13.415 --> 00:56:19.546
Each trooper will learn this operation
and know his mission to the detail.

593
00:56:19.796 --> 00:56:21.590
- Lt. Meehan?
- Yes. Dukeman.

594
00:56:21.840 --> 00:56:25.010
- Are we dropping tonight?
- We'll let you know.

595
00:56:25.260 --> 00:56:29.765
In the meantime. study these
sand tables. maps and recon photos...

596
00:56:30.015 --> 00:56:32.726
...until you can draw a map by memory.

597
00:56:32.976 --> 00:56:35.562
We'll drop behind
this Atlantic Wall...

598
00:56:35.813 --> 00:56:39.525
...five hours before the 4th Infantry
lands at Utah.

599
00:56:39.775 --> 00:56:44.780
Between our assembly area and the
objective. there is a German garrison.

600
00:56:45.030 --> 00:56:47.533
In this area. Sainte-Marie-du-Mont.

601
00:56:47.783 --> 00:56:52.871
Easy Company
will destroy that garrison.

602
00:56:53.497 --> 00:56:57.835
Three-day supply of K rations.
chocolate bars. powdered coffee...

603
00:56:58.085 --> 00:57:01.964
...sugar. matches. compass.
bayonet. ammunition...

604
00:57:02.214 --> 00:57:07.302
...gas mask. musette bag with ammo.
my webbing. my.45. canteen...

605
00:57:07.553 --> 00:57:12.015
...cartons of smokes. Hawkins mine.
smoke grenade. Gammon grenade...

606
00:57:12.266 --> 00:57:15.686
...TNT. this bullshit
and a pair of nasty skivvies.

607
00:57:15.936 --> 00:57:16.979
Your point?

608
00:57:17.229 --> 00:57:21.775
This weighs as much as I do. I still
got my chute. my Mae West and M-1.

609
00:57:22.025 --> 00:57:25.904
- Where are your brass knuckles?
- I could use some.

610
00:57:26.155 --> 00:57:28.615
- Sgt. Martin!
- Vest. anything for me?

611
00:57:28.866 --> 00:57:32.786
Nope. Sgt. Martin!

612
00:57:38.750 --> 00:57:40.085
Talbert!

613
00:57:40.335 --> 00:57:43.297
Floyd. Floyd M.
Here.

614
00:57:43.547 --> 00:57:46.675
- Heavy. Condoms?
- I don't know. probably.

615
00:57:46.925 --> 00:57:50.721
<i>- What you got?
- Dear Floyd: Give them hell.</i>

616
00:57:50.971 --> 00:57:56.143
It's from chief of the Kokomo
Police Department.

617
00:57:57.978 --> 00:57:59.771
You gotta love cops.

618
00:58:00.022 --> 00:58:02.608
All right. listen up! Listen up!

619
00:58:02.858 --> 00:58:06.987
If you did not sign your
GI life insurance policy...

620
00:58:07.237 --> 00:58:12.493
...you go on and see Sgt. Evans
at the Headquarters Company tent.

621
00:58:12.743 --> 00:58:17.122
You boys don't let your families
miss out on $ 10.000.

622
00:58:17.372 --> 00:58:19.041
- You hear. Gerry?
- Lip!

623
00:58:19.291 --> 00:58:22.294
Yeah. boy?

624
00:58:23.378 --> 00:58:26.340
- Has Guarnere mentioned his brother?
- No.

625
00:58:26.590 --> 00:58:28.091
I got a problem.

626
00:58:28.342 --> 00:58:32.804
My wife keeps up with things at home.
Casualty lists and like that.

627
00:58:33.055 --> 00:58:35.933
- Guarnere's brother in Italy...
- Henry?

628
00:58:36.183 --> 00:58:39.353
Killed in Monte Cassino.

629
00:58:39.603 --> 00:58:44.900
- Well. I'm sure he doesn't know.
- Damn. What do you think I should do?

630
00:58:45.150 --> 00:58:51.114
- Lf it were me? I'd tell him.
- A couple hours before we jump?

631
00:58:51.365 --> 00:58:54.034
I don't know.

632
00:59:02.167 --> 00:59:05.128
Why are they springing these
on us now?

633
00:59:05.379 --> 00:59:08.465
It's just 80 extra pounds
strapped to your leg.

634
00:59:08.715 --> 00:59:12.761
Does anybody have any idea
how this thing works?

635
00:59:13.011 --> 00:59:16.056
Colonel Sink.

636
00:59:17.307 --> 00:59:20.352
Colonel Sink.

637
00:59:20.853 --> 00:59:22.855
"Soldiers of the regiment:

638
00:59:23.105 --> 00:59:26.358
Tonight is the night...

639
00:59:26.608 --> 00:59:28.777
...of nights.

640
00:59:29.027 --> 00:59:32.823
As you read this. you are en route
to the adventure...

641
00:59:33.073 --> 00:59:37.286
...for which you have trained
for over two years."

642
00:59:37.536 --> 00:59:41.832
That's why they gave us ice cream.

643
00:59:42.416 --> 00:59:46.920
Easy Company! Listen up!

644
00:59:47.296 --> 00:59:50.257
Channel coast is socked in
with rain and fog.

645
00:59:50.507 --> 00:59:53.135
No jump tonight.

646
00:59:53.385 --> 01:00:00.809
The invasion has been postponed.
We're on a 24-hour stand-down.

647
01:00:30.839 --> 01:00:34.343
"Dearest Johnny"?

648
01:00:38.263 --> 01:00:42.643
I got the wrong goddamn jacket.

649
01:00:54.905 --> 01:00:58.575
"Bill Guarnere's brother..."

650
01:02:30.792 --> 01:02:33.420
- Good luck. lads.
- See you. Tommy.

651
01:02:33.670 --> 01:02:37.090
Give Jerry one for me.

652
01:02:55.400 --> 01:02:58.487
Johnny.

653
01:03:03.116 --> 01:03:05.369
You might be looking for this.

654
01:03:05.619 --> 01:03:08.622
I took your jacket by mistake.
I'm sorry.

655
01:03:08.872 --> 01:03:12.000
You read it?

656
01:03:12.417 --> 01:03:18.966
- Where the fuck is Monte Cassino?
- I don't know. Italy somewhere.

657
01:03:20.175 --> 01:03:22.719
Sorry about your brother. Bill.

658
01:03:22.970 --> 01:03:25.472
I'm sorry for my ma.

659
01:03:25.722 --> 01:03:29.017
He was...

660
01:03:31.645 --> 01:03:34.940
Let's get this over with.

661
01:03:37.359 --> 01:03:39.987
Bill?

662
01:03:41.613 --> 01:03:45.784
I'll meet up with you over there.

663
01:03:47.828 --> 01:03:50.706
Doc Roe is giving these out
for airsickness.

664
01:03:50.956 --> 01:03:56.253
Orders are. every man takes one now.
Another. 30 minutes in the air.

665
01:03:56.503 --> 01:03:59.464
Lieutenant.

666
01:04:04.386 --> 01:04:08.432
2nd Platoon. listen up.

667
01:04:09.641 --> 01:04:12.227
Good luck.

668
01:04:12.478 --> 01:04:15.814
God bless you.

669
01:04:15.814 --> 01:04:20.360
I'll see you in the assembly area.

670
01:05:12.704 --> 01:05:19.086
If the wire cuts are successful.
all we should have to deal with is...

671
01:05:22.381 --> 01:05:28.262
- Goddamn. Lieb.
- That airsick pill is making me loopy.

672
01:05:29.305 --> 01:06:29.495
Do you want subtitles for any video?
-=[ ai.OpenSubtitles.com ]=-
